# The API-facing calculator (issue #38)

`ApiCalculator` is the one reference mapping between the JSON API
(`api/schema.json`, `docs/api.md`) and the whole-return scope `Calculator`
(`catala/calculator.catala_en`). Its input `request` is the API request
(`CalculateRequest`) after the JSON decoding step that `docs/api-mapping.md`
specifies; its outputs are the fields of the API response:

| Output | API response field |
|---|---|
| `supported` | `supported` (false: HTTP 422 `CalculateUnsupported`) |
| `reasons` | `reasons[]`: `code` is the name of the constructor (the one inside `IncomeOrHsa` for an income, HSA or process knockout), `category` the snake_case of the `ApiReasonCategory` constructor |
| `outcome` | `outcome`: `Refund` is `refund`, `BalanceDue` is `balance_due`, `Even` is `even` |
| `lines` | `lines` (nineteen Form 1040 line items) |

Calculator takes no part of the request on faith: every request field is
mapped here, either into a `Calculator` input or (for the legacy
`filing_details` flags that `Calculator` derives itself) documented below.

## Units: cents on the wire, dollars here

The API carries every money value as an integer number of cents (docs/api.md,
"Money: integer cents"). Catala `money` is a decimal amount of dollars with
cent precision, so the JSON decoding step (not this file) divides each money
field by 100 on the way in (`5000000` becomes `$50,000.00`) and multiplies each
`lines` field by 100 on the way out. The conversion is exact: no rounding
happens on the wire. `Calculator` rounds every box and line to whole dollars as
Direct File does (CONVENTIONS section 4), so every `lines` value is a whole
number of dollars, a multiple of 100 cents.

## Absent means a documented default

An API request leaves out optional properties. The decoding step fills each
absent property with the `default` of `api/schema.json` (false, 0, the empty
list, or the named constructor) before this scope sees it, so `Api_calculator`
inputs are complete. Two kinds of default depend on the rest of the request and
are decided here, not by the decoder:

- an absent `date_of_birth` (decoder: `date_of_birth_given` is false): the
  filer is born 1950-06-15 if `age65_or_older` (so 74 at the end of 2024),
  else 1985-06-15;
- an absent `marital_status` or `year_of_spouse_death` (the constructor
  `Unspecified`): derived from the filing status, see `MaritalOf` below.

## The legacy `filing_details` flags (schema 1.0 and 1.1)

Schema 1.0 took the standard deduction's answers as inputs. `Calculator`
derives them from the filers' facts, so they map as follows. Nothing is
silently dropped: `docs/api-mapping.md` lists each one.

| Legacy field | Now |
|---|---|
| `treat_as_mfs` | ignored: it is `filing_status = MarriedFilingSeparately` |
| `is_widowed_in_tax_year` | `marital_status` Widowed and `year_of_spouse_death` `DiedInTaxYear` when those are `Unspecified` |
| `mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65` | the secondary filer counts as 65 or older (when no date of birth is given) |
| `mfs_spouse_65_or_older` | passed to `Filers.mfs_spouse_65_or_older` |
| `mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits` | counts as `mfs_spouse_has_gross_income` |
| `treat_filers_as_dependents` | both filers can be claimed, will be claimed, and the claimer must file |
| `has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts` | or-ed into `screening.has_foreign_accounts` |
| `combat_pay_election` | `income.combat_pay_election`; `combat_pay_election_made` is true when it is not `NoCombatPay` |
| `social_security.lived_apart_all_year` | the spouses did not live together at any time: `lived_together_all_year_with_spouse` false and `spouse_lived_together_months` `LivedApartAllYear` |

## API structures

```catala-metadata
## The marital status the filer reports; `Unspecified` takes the default of the
## filing status (see `MaritalOf`).
declaration enumeration ApiMaritalStatus:
  -- Unspecified
  -- NeverMarried
  -- Married
  -- Divorced
  -- Widowed

declaration enumeration ApiYearOfSpouseDeath:
  -- Unspecified
  -- DiedInTaxYear
  -- DiedTaxYearMinusOne
  -- DiedTaxYearMinusTwo
  -- DiedBeforeTaxYearMinusTwo

## API `filers.primary` and `filers.secondary` (schema `FilerFlags`).
declaration structure ApiFiler:
  data is_blind content boolean
  data age65_or_older content boolean
  data can_be_claimed_as_dependent content boolean
  # The decoder sets this to whether the request had `date_of_birth`
  data date_of_birth_given content boolean
  data date_of_birth content date
  data will_be_claimed content boolean
  data potential_claimer_must_file content boolean
  data potential_claimer_did_file content boolean
  data is_us_citizen_full_year content boolean
  data citizen_at_end_of_tax_year content boolean
  data noncitizen_resident_full_year content boolean
  data is_national content boolean
  data is_student content boolean
  data tin content Calc.FilerTin
  data disability content ED.DisabilityAnswers
  data hsa content H.HsaFilerAnswers
  data cdcc content Calc.CdccFilerAnswers

declaration structure ApiFilers:
  data primary content ApiFiler
  data secondary content ApiFiler

## API `filing_details` (the 1.0 fields, plus `combat_pay_election_made`).
declaration structure ApiFilingDetails:
  data treat_as_mfs content boolean
  data is_widowed_in_tax_year content boolean
  data mfj_deceased_spouse_reached_age65 content boolean
  data mfs_spouse_65_or_older content boolean
  data mfs_spouse_provides_no_benefits content boolean
  data treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  data has_foreign_accounts_or_trusts content boolean
  data combat_pay_election content W.CombatPayElection
  data combat_pay_election_made content boolean

## API `filing_answers` (schema 1.2.0): the marital and residence answers
## `Filers.Filers` reads.
declaration structure ApiFilingAnswers:
  data marital_status content ApiMaritalStatus
  data year_of_spouse_death content ApiYearOfSpouseDeath
  data secondary_filer_date_of_death content date
  data primary_filer_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund content boolean
  data mfj_required_to_file content boolean
  data mfj_dependents_filing_for_credits content boolean
  data lived_together_all_year_with_spouse content boolean
  data spouse_lived_together_months content F.SpouseLivedTogetherMonths
  data lived_apart_last_six_months content boolean
  data separation_agreement content boolean
  data can_file_jointly_year_of_spouse_death content boolean
  data in_registered_domestic_partnership content boolean
  data residence_state content Types.ScopedState
  data spouse_itemizes content boolean
  data mfs_living_spouse_filing_return content boolean
  data mfs_deceased_spouse_filing_return content boolean
  data mfs_spouse_has_gross_income content boolean

## API `dependents[]` (schema 1.2.0): one household member with the Direct
## File per-person facts (`/familyAndHousehold/*`), flat. Money in dollars here.
declaration structure ApiDependent:
  data relationship content Q.Relationship
  data date_of_birth content date
  data full_time_student content boolean
  data permanent_total_disability content boolean
  data residency_duration content Q.ResidencyDuration
  data own_support content boolean
  data married content boolean
  data joint_return content boolean
  data required_to_file content boolean
  data filing_only_for_refund content boolean
  data could_be_qualifying_child_of_another content boolean
  data potential_claimer_must_file content boolean
  data potential_claimer_did_file content boolean
  data potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund content boolean
  data gross_income content money
  data qr_support_test content boolean
  data tin_type content QR.TinType
  data is_us_citizen_full_year content boolean
  data us_resident content boolean
  data us_national content boolean
  data canada_mexico_resident content boolean
  data tp_claims content boolean
  data deceased content boolean
  data custody content B.BenefitSplitAnswers
  data tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep content boolean
  data tp_paid_most_of_parent_home_upkeep content boolean
  data ssn_employment_validity content C.SsnEmploymentValidity
  data ssn_only_for_federally_funded_benefit content boolean
  data months_lived_with_tp_in_us content integer
  data cdcc content Calc.CdccMemberAnswers

## API `screening` (1.2.0): `Calculator.ScreeningAnswers` without `member_vitals`, which
## is derived from `dependents[]` (date of birth, `deceased`, `tin_type` NoTin).
declaration structure ApiScreening:
  data income_sources_supported content boolean
  data received_digital_assets content boolean
  data disposed_digital_assets content boolean
  data has_foreign_accounts content boolean
  data is_foreign_trusts_grantor content boolean
  data has_foreign_trusts_transactions content boolean
  data made_ira_contributions content boolean
  data w2_box15_income_from_different_state content boolean
  data w2_has_box14_nyrrta_knockout_code content boolean
  data w2_has_rrta_codes_in_box14 content boolean
  data lived_in_ny content boolean
  data w2_paid_yonkers_taxes content boolean
  data part_year_yonkers_resident content boolean
  data primary_filer_forms_another_state content boolean
  data received_alaska_pfd content boolean
  data spouse_received_alaska_pfd content boolean
  data spouse_lives_in_other_or_multiple_states content boolean
  data spouse_forms_another_state content boolean
  data is_after_tax_day_and_not_resubmitting content boolean
  data is_after_resubmission_deadline content boolean

## API `social_security`.
declaration structure ApiSocialSecurity:
  data net_benefits content list of money
  data federal_tax_withheld content list of money
  data lived_apart_all_year content boolean

declaration structure ApiEducator:
  data was_k12_educators content EA.K12EducatorOptions
  data primary_expenses content money
  data secondary_expenses content money

declaration structure ApiStudentLoan:
  data had_payments content boolean
  data loans_qualify content boolean
  data interest_amount content money

## API `adjustments`: educator expenses, student loan interest, and (1.2.0) HSA.
declaration structure ApiAdjustments:
  data educator_expenses content ApiEducator
  data student_loan_interest content ApiStudentLoan
  data hsa content Calc.HsaInput

declaration structure ApiEstimatedPayments:
  data paid_estimated_taxes_or_from_last_year content boolean
  data amount content money
  data paid_under_different_name content boolean
  data paid_with_former_spouse content EP.PaidWithFormerSpouse

```

